.TH GET 1 "2026-09-21" "get 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
get \- get anything from your computer
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B get
.RI \(dq query \(dq
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B get set
.I option
.RI [ value ]
.br
.B get config
.RI [ \-\-reset | \-\- option ]
.br
.B get cache
.RI [ \-\-clean | "\-\-unset \(dq" query \(dq ]
.br
.B get log
.RI [ \-\-clean ]
.br
.B get get
.RI [ \-\-name | \-\-intro | \-\-version | \-\-author | \-\-license | \-\-github ]
.br
.B get version
.br
.B get \-\-version
.br
.B get \-V
.br
.B get isok
.br
.B get help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get
sends a natural-language query to an OpenAI-compatible model and performs
read-only local inspection when a shell command is required.
Version 4 uses one typed
.I model/action/policy/tool/observation
state machine instead of separate instance and marker-driven agent paths.
.PP
Provider-native function tools are preferred.
Structured JSON is used as a compatibility fallback. Markdown code blocks and
old HTML action markers are answer text. Legacy configuration values migrate
to the JSON protocol. Model names are opaque identifiers, without rankings.
.PP
Queries that explicitly request no tool use are routed as text-only: no tool
definition is sent, textual tool actions are rejected, and cached commands are
ignored.
.PP
Every proposed, revised, or cached command passes through the same mandatory
read-only policy, optional supplemental regex, optional model review, optional
manual confirmation, and bounded executor.
.
.SH HARNESS STRATEGIES
.TP
.B auto
Default. Inspects local facts and then answers using the observations. A denied
command is not executed. The model may select another reader within the
inspection budget; a separate final answer turn has no tools.
.TP
.B direct
Exactly one model turn and at most one terminal tool call.
.TP
.B loop
Feeds observations back serially for dependent multi-step work.
.TP
.B parallel
Allows independent read-only calls to execute concurrently, up to
.BR max\-parallel .
.PP
All strategies share the same state machine and hard budgets.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Query (default)"
.BI "get \(dq" query "\(dq [" flags "]"
.PP
Runs the query using the configured harness.
.
.SS set
.BI "get set " option " [" value ]
.PP
Sets one persistent option. Omitting the value resets it to its default or
clears a string value.
.
.SS config
.B get config
.PP
Displays settings. The API key is shown only as set or not set.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Restores defaults and removes the stored key.
.TP
.BI \-\- option
Displays one setting.
.
.SS cache
.B get cache
.PP
Displays cache counts, limits, and file location.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Removes all entries.
.TP
.BI "\-\-unset \(dq" query \(dq
Removes entries matching the query text.
.
.SS log
.B get log
.PP
Displays log status and location.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Removes all log entries.
.
.SS get
.B get get
.PP
Displays application metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-name
Show the application name.
.TP
.B \-\-intro
Show the introduction.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version 4.0.0.
.TP
.B \-\-author
Show the author.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Show the SPDX license identifier.
.TP
.B \-\-github
Show the repository URL.
.
.SS version
.B get version
.PP
Displays version 4.0.0. The standard aliases
.B \-\-version
and
.B \-V
are equivalent and do not require provider configuration.
.
.SS isok
.B get isok
.PP
Checks key, URL, and model, then sends a minimal provider request.
.
.SH QUERY FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cache lookup and storage.
.TP
.B \-\-cache
Force cache use and permit terminal text-result storage.
.TP
.B \-\-manual\-confirm
Prompt before every command.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-manual\-confirm
Skip interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-double\-check
Enable an additional model safety review.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-double\-check
Skip the additional review. The mandatory deterministic policy still runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-harness " kind"
Use auto, direct, loop, or parallel for this query.
.TP
.BI \-\-protocol " kind"
Use auto, native, or json tool encoding for this query.
.TP
.B \-\-instance
Compatibility alias for direct.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-instance
Compatibility alias for loop.
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-process
Suppress progress and intermediate observations.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hide\-process
Show progress and observations.
.TP
.B \-\-system\-proxy
Prefer enabled Windows Internet Settings over terminal proxy variables.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-system\-proxy
Use terminal proxy variables only.
.TP
.B \-\-vivid
Enable ANSI styling.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-vivid
Use plain text.
.TP
.B \-\-markdown
Render model Markdown in an interactive terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-markdown
Display the original Markdown source.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " name"
Override the model.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Override the API request timeout.
.
.SH SET OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "key " string
API key. Linux storage uses mode 0600; Windows uses DPAPI. Default: empty.
.TP
.BI "url " URL
API base URL. Default: https://api.minimaxi.com/v1.
.TP
.BI "model " string
Model identifier. Default: minimax-m3.
.TP
.BI "manual\-confirm " bool
Interactive command confirmation. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "double\-check " bool
Second model review. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "harness " kind
auto, direct, loop, or parallel. Default: auto.
.TP
.BI "tool\-protocol " kind
auto, native, or json. Default: auto.
.TP
.BI "timeout " "int | false"
API timeout seconds. Default: 300.
.TP
.BI "max\-token " "int | false"
Maximum response tokens. Default: 20480.
.TP
.BI "max\-rounds " int
Inspection-turn limit plus one tool-free final answer turn. Default: 6.
.TP
.BI "max\-tool\-calls " int
Actual tool-start limit per query. Default: 16.
.TP
.BI "max\-parallel " int
Maximum concurrent tool calls. Default: 4.
.TP
.BI "query\-timeout " int
Whole automatic query deadline, including model and tools. Default: 120.
.TP
.BI "diagnostics " bool
Structured query events and counters on stderr. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "command\-timeout " int
Hard command deadline in seconds. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI "max\-output\-bytes " int
Per-command capture cap. Default: 1048576.
.TP
.BI "command\-pattern " regex
Supplemental forbidden-command regex. Omitting the value restores the built-in
semantic-policy-only default. An explicit empty string clears an existing
supplemental regex; the mandatory read-only policy remains active.
.TP
.BI "system\-prompt " string
Additional model instruction. Default: empty.
.TP
.BI "shell " string
Shell executable. Default: bash on Unix, powershell on Windows.
.TP
.BI "log " bool
Execution logging. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "hide\-process " bool
Suppress intermediate output. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "system\-proxy " bool
Prefer Windows Internet Settings over terminal proxy variables. Default: false.
.TP
.BI "cache " bool
Deterministic caching. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "cache\-expiry " "int | false"
Cache lifetime in days. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI "cache\-max\-entries " "int | false"
Cache entry cap. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI "log\-max\-entries " "int | false"
Log entry cap. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI "vivid " bool
ANSI styling and animation. Default: true.
.TP
.BI "markdown " bool
Render model answers in interactive terminals. Default: true.
Pipes, redirected output, TERM=dumb, and raw command output retain source text.
NO_COLOR or vivid=false disables renderer colors, while preserving layout.
Cached answers are rendered using the current setting.
.TP
.BI "instance " bool
v2 compatibility alias. true selects direct; false selects auto when stored.
.
.SH TOOL PROTOCOL
The native tools are read_environment, read_file, search_files, run_process,
and run_shell. They accept typed names, paths, paging arguments, literal argv,
or a shell command respectively. required/evidence_key identify essential
facts; fresh requests a new sample. run_readonly_shell is a compatibility alias.
.PP
With tool-protocol auto, provider HTTP 400/404/422 errors that identify
unsupported tool fields trigger one structured-JSON retry for that run.
Native mode does not fall back. Legacy mode sends no native tool definition.
.PP
Transport failures before an HTTP response retry up to three times within the
original request timeout. HTTP responses, request timeouts, and parsing errors
are not retried. Provider response bodies are limited to 8 MiB, and requests
carrying bearer credentials do not follow redirects.
.
.SH SAFETY
Typed environment and file readers do not execute shell text. Files are paged;
search implements bounded literal content matching, path globs, and common
ignore rules. Missing values, no matches, and incomplete pages are explicit.
.PP
Known host queries validate executable arguments and observe real host state.
General scripts and complex shell computation are enabled only on Linux when
the complete isolation probe succeeds. Namespaces, read-only host mounts,
seccomp and resource limits restrict writes to private scratch space and block
network/control sockets, host process control and device control. The parent
cleans scratch space. macOS and Windows provide typed readers and known host
queries; arbitrary computation is unavailable there.
.PP
Ordinary Git status/diff use a private metadata snapshot without writing the
real index. Executable filters, textconv, fsmonitor and submodule inspection
are disabled. Global excludes, upstream settings and custom filtered results
may differ from interactive Git; the observation identifies its source.
.PP
All new, reviewed and cached plans share argument validation, backend selection,
optional command-pattern restrictions, optional double-check and optional
manual-confirm. Confirmation does not enable host mutation. Trusted shell
startup hooks and injection variables are removed from child environments.
.PP
Rejections and reused observations do not spend execution slots. A failed step
can recover within the total budget, with at most two failure-recovery turns.
Necessary evidence failures remain nonzero even when the model returns prose.
stdout and stderr are separate; feedback compaction and actual capture
truncation have distinct flags. fresh permits bounded repeat sampling.
.PP
Automatic execution uses query-timeout, command-timeout and max-output-bytes.
Model requests and queued tools receive only the remaining deadline. A final
answer turn reserves time and has no tools. Explicit interactive confirmation
can wait for user input; no tool starts after its execution deadline.
.PP
The query boundary resists mutation, not disclosure. Requested observations
may be sent to the configured provider. Environment credential values are
redacted, but arbitrary file content is not a universal secret filter.
Host readers depend on trusted programs and configuration; reads may update
access metadata. HTTP readers permit checked GET/HEAD forms, whose remote
semantics depend on the server.
.
.SH CACHE
The v4 cache performs no classifier model call. Schema 4 stores typed plans.
A successful single-step raw query stores a context-specific typed plan.
A hit uses zero model calls, validates the command again, and re-executes it.
This keeps dynamic information current.
An explicit text-only request never executes a cached command, though a cached
final text result may still be returned without a model or tool call.
.PP
Cache identities use SHA-256 over the provider, model, strategy, protocol,
shell, policy, tool/backend capabilities, execution limits, platform, and working-directory context. Writers serialize the
complete read-modify-write operation with a cross-process lock. Snapshots are
flushed, atomically replaced, and backed by a last-good copy used when the
primary is damaged. Cache files and individual fields are size-bounded and
schema-validated.
.PP
The \-\-cache flag may store a terminal text answer when no reusable command
exists; hits show its original sample time. Multi-step results are not guessed into cache entries.
Versioned keys include working directory, provider URL, model, harness,
protocol, shell, custom prompt, policy configuration, OS, and architecture.
.
.SH NETWORK
All model turns reuse one TLS-verifying HTTP client, including proxy traffic.
Certificate chains and DNS/IP host names are verified. On Windows, get imports
the native Windows ROOT certificate store into OpenSSL; no separate CA bundle
is required for ordinary HTTPS.
Terminal proxy variables are respected by default. When system-proxy is true,
enabled Windows Internet Settings take precedence. NO_PROXY/no_proxy bypasses
either source. Credentials are redacted when a proxy URL is displayed.
.PP
NO_PROXY entries are comma-separated. Domains match themselves and their
subdomains; IP literals match the exact address; a single * bypasses all proxies.
An entry without a port applies to every port. A host:port entry applies only
to that destination port, using HTTP 80 or HTTPS 443 when the URL omits it.
IPv6 may use ::1 or [::1]; an IPv6 port requires brackets, as in [::1]:8080.
Entries with empty, nonnumeric, or out-of-range ports (outside 1-65535) are
ignored without broadening the bypass to the whole host.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/config.json
Linux configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/key
Linux API key file, mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/cache.json
Cache store.
.TP
.I ~/.config/get/get.log
Execution log.
.PP
On Windows these files are under %APPDATA%\eget and the key is DPAPI-protected.
The release installer also places the required OpenSSL runtime DLLs beside the
Windows executable.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, provider, protocol, policy, refusal, budget, or general error.
.TP
.B 124
Command deadline exceeded.
.TP
.B 126
Tool proposal rejected before execution with no safe revision inside budget.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B other
Exit status of a terminal command.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
get \(dqcurrent directory\(dq
get \(dqcompare disk and memory usage\(dq \-\-harness parallel
get \(dqservice status\(dq \-\-double\-check
get set tool\-protocol native
get set max\-parallel 6
get cache \-\-clean
.fi
.
